# {{ _copier_conf.dst_path.name }}

A [Mistral Search Toolkit](https://pypi.org/project/mistralai-search-toolkit/) project with a Postgres (pgvector) backend.

SDK namespace: `mistralai.search.toolkit` — see the [toolkit docs](https://github.com/mistralai/mistral-pro/tree/main/dashboards/main/search/toolkit) for architecture and extension guides.

## Setup

```bash
make installdeps
```

`MISTRAL_API_KEY` is set in `.env` from the value you entered during `copier copy` (or edit `.env` later). Project name matches the folder you passed to `copier copy` (this directory).

The Postgres connection string lives in `.env` as `POSTGRES_DSN` (defaults to the
local dev container: `postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/postgres`).

## Commands

### Start Postgres and create the schema

```bash
make setup-postgres
```

This starts the `pgvector/pgvector:pg18` container (port **5432**) and then runs
`make create-schema`, which creates the `vector` extension and the table backing
`COLLECTION_NAME` (idempotent — safe to rerun).

To wipe local Postgres data and start fresh:

```bash
make reset-postgres
make setup-postgres
```

### Ingest documents

Uses two `Pipeline` instances (plain-text vs OCR) shared across a file or directory ingest. Text files use `PlainTextExtractor`; other files (e.g. PDFs) use `MistralOCRExtractor` (requires `MISTRAL_API_KEY`).

```bash
make ingest path=sample_data/hello.txt
make ingest path=sample_data
```

### Search the collection

Uses `QueryEngine` with `VectorRetriever` (dense vector search via pgvector):

```bash
make search query="hello world"
```

Postgres search is dense top-k only — there are no Vespa-style query profiles, so
there is no `query_profile=` option.

## Project layout

```
src/
├── entrypoints/
│   ├── ingest.py          # mistralai.search.toolkit.ingestion.pipelines.Pipeline
│   ├── search.py          # mistralai.search.toolkit.retrieval.QueryEngine
│   └── postgres_create_schema.py   # CREATE EXTENSION vector + create table
└── search_app/
    └── __init__.py        # PostgresApp — mistralai.search.toolkit.plugins.postgres
sample_data/               # Sample documents
```

## Development

```bash
uv run ruff format .
uv run ruff check --fix .
```
